cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "CENE: Context-Enforcement Network Engine"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rastogi
    given-names: Vaibhav
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0900-4376"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Melbourne, Australia"
version: 1.0.0
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: 2026-11-13
abstract: >-
  CENE enforces an AI agent's scope outside the model: data-quality tiers set the agent's authority, a short-lived
  signed Context Token lists the tools, arguments and rows a task may use, a gateway checks every tool call
  (refusing, or holding for two approvers) and a hash-chained audit log records every decision. Includes the
  AgentDojo evaluation (frozen policy agentdojo-policy-v1) with Gemma 4 12B-it and Qwen3-8B.
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - prompt injection
  - tool-call enforcement
  - AgentDojo
  - audit
